1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
RetailPulse AI: a personal portfolio for traceable retail demand analytics.
Historical sales, not a live customer deployment.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Commercial managers, BI analysts and planners need consistent figures
to compare stores, investigate changes and review forecast error.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:32,000
M5 flows through Bronze, Silver and Gold in DuckDB.
Frozen forecasting, Power BI and the application share that source.

4
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Lineage ties each result to its source and period.
Serving reads approved data; opening this demo does not train models.

5
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:58,000
The real historical pilot contains 4,530,250 observed units.
The date range and stored snapshot date remain visible.

6
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Filtering to CA_1 shows 1,477,827 historical units.
The same definitions serve the dashboard and the API.

7
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Missing prices remain missing. Known-price revenue is only a partial proxy.
Reset all stores before comparing the full-pilot models.

8
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Frozen test WMAPE: LightGBM 74.825958%; rolling mean 79.482353%.
Selection used validation only, before this test was opened.

9
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:45,000
MAE improves, but RMSE worsens: 2.431177 versus 2.361194.
This trade-off is not a claim of measured revenue gains.

10
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Ask: How many units did CA_1 sell during April 2016?
This recording uses explicit deterministic offline operation.

11
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:05,000
25,307 units, with the period, store and Gold source attached.
Approved read-only tools supply the number.

12
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:15,000
The bounded router establishes scope; optional Ollama only confirms it.
This offline answer is not counted as a live model call.

13
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Recorded engineering evidence: 254 tests, 88.15% combined coverage,
and successful required Windows, Linux and Docker checks.

14
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Historical data, no actual inventory and no public production deployment.
Independent human setup and release approval remain pending; AWS is deferred.
